/* 段落记忆 · 词层 3 · 子块 b：词头 → {tw:[关系词,关系类型], en, zh} */
window.APP_MERGE_NET(3,{"sub":"b","par":{"dominate":{"tw":[["dominant",4],["dominance",4],["dominion",4],["possess",3],["rule",0],["master",0],["shadow",3],["control",2],["lie",2]],"en":"For almost fifty years one family seemed to dominate the cloth trade in the valley. Their dominance was so complete that other makers could not sell a single roll of cloth, and their dominion reached every village along the river. They would possess the best machines and rule the prices from a single office, and theirs was the dominant voice in every meeting. The old master of the biggest workshop liked to say that a good merchant must watch the market the way a farmer watches the sky. Under his shadow, small shops opened and closed within a season. Today a young designer works to take control of the trade with a small computer and a fast website. The first step, she says, is to lie less about quality.","zh":"差不多五十年里，山谷里的布匹生意一直由一户人家说了算。他们势大得让别的作坊连一匹布都卖不出去，势力范围一直铺到河边的每个村子。最好的机器归他们，价格也从一间办公室里定下来。最大那家作坊的老掌柜爱说，好商人看市场，得像农夫看天。在他的影子下，小铺子开一季就关。如今一位年轻设计师正想靠一台小电脑和一个快网站把这门生意接过来。她说，第一步就是少在质量上撒谎。"},"foundation":{"tw":[["base",0],["bed",3],["footing",3],["charity",3],["institute",6],["support",2],["basis",0],["assumption",2],["foot",0]],"en":"The new school stands on a wide concrete foundation. Workers dug the base two metres into the brown earth, below the level of the river bed. The engineers say the whole building rests on the right footing because of that first layer. The money came from a charity and from a small institute that studies village education. Their support was the basis of the plan, and the assumption behind it was simple: children learn better in a building they helped to design. Today the head teacher points at the stone at the foot of the steps and says that every good lesson stands on the same thing.","zh":"新学校立在一大片混凝土基础上。工人把基座挖进褐色的土里两米深，比河床还低。工程师说，正因为有了这第一层，整栋楼才站得稳。钱来自一家慈善机构和一个研究乡村教育的小研究所。他们的支持是这个方案的基础，而方案背后的假设很简单：孩子在自己参与设计的楼里学得更好。如今校长指着台阶脚下那块石头说，每一堂好课靠的都是同样的东西。"},"deposit":{"tw":[["deposition",4],["drop",3],["fix",0],["matter",2],["stick",0],["lodge",0],["fund",2],["margin",3],["withdraw",1]],"en":"The geologist came to study the thin deposit of salt on the rock. The deposition had taken thousands of years, and a single drop of water could fix the grains together again. She used a knife to take a sample and watched the white matter stick to her fingers. That evening she had to lodge a report with the town office before the fund for the survey closed. There was no margin for a second trip. The next morning she went to withdraw the money, and the clerk asked where the salt had come from. 'From a sea that is not here any more,' she said.","zh":"地质学家来研究岩石上那薄薄一层盐的沉积。这些沉积物积了上千年，而一滴水就能让盐粒重新粘在一起。她用刀取了个样，看着白色的东西黏在手指上。那天傍晚她得赶在调查经费截止前把报告交付到镇公所。再跑一趟的余地是没有了。第二天早上她去取钱，办事员问她这盐从哪儿来。她说：'来自一片已经不在这里的海。'"},"expert":{"tw":[["professor",6],["research",6],["technical",0],["technician",3],["adept",0],["veteran",3],["scout",3],["forensic",6]],"en":"The old professor is an expert on soil. He spent forty years in research, and his technical knowledge fills twelve notebooks. His expertise came from walking the same fields again and again in every season. A young technician once asked him how to read a weak signal from a broken machine, and he was adept enough to find the fault in a minute. Next to him stood a veteran scout who knew every path in the hills. The two men had little in common, yet they talked for hours about the same problem. That autumn the police called a forensic team to the valley, and the professor's old notes helped them understand what the water had carried away.","zh":"那位老教授是土壤方面的专家。他做了四十年研究，技术上的积累写满了十二个笔记本。他的专长来自一季又一季在同一片地里来回走。有个年轻技师问他，怎么从一台坏机器的微弱信号里看出问题，他熟到一分钟就找到了故障。站在他旁边的是一位老兵侦察员，山里的每条小路他都清楚。这两个人几乎没什么共同点，却就同一个问题聊了几个钟头。那年秋天，警方请了一队法证人员到山谷来，教授当年的笔记帮他们弄明白了水把什么冲走了。"},"execute":{"tw":[["executive",4],["run",0],["carry",3],["complete",2],["prosecute",6],["executor",4],["perform",0],["kill",2],["proceed",6],["accomplish",0]],"en":"The old man's will named my aunt as executor, and her first duty was to execute his wishes exactly. A bank executive helped her read the long papers. She had to run the small farm for one more season and carry the accounts to the town office. The lawyer would prosecute anyone who tried to hide money from the estate. A judge said the case could not proceed until every paper was complete. My aunt agreed to perform each task herself and to accomplish them within a year. She would never kill a promise her father had made. That spring the work was finally done, and the family could rest.","zh":"老人的遗嘱指定我姑妈做遗嘱执行人，她的头一桩事，就是严格照他的意愿去执行。银行里一位高管帮她读了那些长长的文件。她得再把那个小农场经营一季，还要把账目送到镇公所。哪个亲属想从遗产里藏钱，律师都会起诉他。法官说，材料不齐，案子就不能往下走。姑妈答应每件事都亲自去做，并在一年之内办完。她绝不会毁掉父亲许下的诺言。那个春天，事情终于了结，一家人也松了口气。"},"descend":{"tw":[["descent",4],["fall",0],["dive",3],["act",2],["ascend",1],["wander",6],["settle",0],["pitch",3],["travel",2],["converge",6],["derive",0]],"en":"At noon we began to descend from the high ridge toward the valley. The descent was steep, and twice I had to sit down to keep from a fall. My brother would dive ahead like a goat, then wander off the path to look at the rocks. As we went lower, small streams began to converge into one wider river. We had to pitch our tent before dark, and it took an act of patience to get the poles straight. That night we would travel no further; we chose to settle by the water. Much of the valley water seems to derive from the snow above. In the morning we would do the harder job and ascend.","zh":"中午时分，我们开始从高高的山脊往山谷下走。下坡很陡，我有两次不得不坐下来，免得摔下去。我弟弟像只山羊似的往前冲，一会儿又偏离小路去看那些石头。越往下走，几条小溪开始汇聚成一条更宽的河。我们得赶在天黑前把帐篷支起来，把杆子弄直需要一点耐心的功夫。那一晚我们不再赶路了；我们决定就在水边安顿下来。山谷里的水，多半像是从上面的雪里来的。第二天早上，我们还要干更累的活——往山上爬。"},"expand":{"tw":[["expansion",4],["boom",0],["detail",3],["change",2],["contract",1],["enable",6],["extend",0],["develop",3],["grow",2],["boost",6],["elaborate",0]],"en":"Three years ago my uncle decided to expand his small repair shop. At first he had to explain every detail of his plan to the bank, and he would elaborate on the numbers for an hour. The manager agreed to extend him a loan, which would enable him to buy two new machines. Business began to grow, and a short boom in the town helped. We watched the slow expansion of the yard as more cars arrived. The old contracts had to change, and some workers worried about the cost. A small poster helped boost sales that summer. Step by step, the shop developed into a real service station.","zh":"三年前，我叔叔决定把他那家小修理铺扩大。起初，他不得不向银行把计划的每个细节都讲清楚，还花了一个钟头细说那些数字。经理同意给他放贷，这样他就能买两台新机器。生意开始红火起来，镇上的一阵景气也帮了忙。随着车越来越多，我们看着院子慢慢扩建。老合同得改，有些工人为成本发愁。那年夏天，一张小海报帮着把销路提了上去。一步一步，这个小铺子发展成了一家像样的服务站。"},"focus":{"tw":[["focal",4],["centre",0],["listen",3],["think",2],["blur",1],["aim",6],["concentrate",0],["recall",3],["adjust",2],["future",6],["direction",0]],"en":"On the morning of the exam I could not focus at all. My eyes would blur, and I could not recall a single date. Instead of studying, I sat by the window and let my thoughts run in every direction. Then I decided to change my aim: take a short walk and listen to the birds outside. I sat on a bench in the centre of the park and tried to concentrate on one small thing at a time. I had to adjust my plan for the week and think about the future in a calmer way. That simple walk became the focal point of my whole week. When I returned to the desk, the words finally came.","zh":"考试那天早上，我根本没法集中注意力。眼睛发花，一个日期都想不起来。我没再死看书，而是坐到窗边，任思绪朝四面八方跑。后来我决定换个目标：出去走一小段，听听外面的鸟叫。我坐在公园中央的长椅上，试着一次只专心在一件小事上。我只好调整这一周的计划，用更平静的心态去想将来。那趟短短的散步，竟成了我整个星期关注的焦点。等我回到书桌前，词句终于来了。"},"defend":{"tw":[["defence",4],["guard",0],["protect",3],["argue",2],["attack",1],["intend",6],["defendant",4],["resist",3],["prevent",2]],"en":"In court that morning a young lawyer rose to defend a quiet shopkeeper. She did not intend to attack the other side; she simply wanted to argue the facts. Her defence was simple: her client had been at home when the fire began. The defendant sat still and did not resist any question. The lawyer called an old guard from the yard, who had tried to protect the door. She asked him to explain what he saw and to prevent the court from a wrong idea. The judge listened for an hour. By noon the whole room seemed to believe her.","zh":"那天上午在法庭上，一位年轻律师站起来为一位沉默的店主辩护。她并不想攻击对方；她只想就事实展开论辩。她的辩词很简单：起火时她的当事人正在家里。被告静静坐着，对任何问题都不抗拒。律师传了院子里一位老门卫上庭，那人曾试图护住那扇门。她请他讲清自己看到了什么，别让法庭听信错误的说法。法官听了一个钟头。到中午，满屋子的人似乎都信了她。"},"grave":{"tw":[["gravity",4],["heavy",0],["death",2],["damage",6],["gravely",4],["serious",5],["accent",2],["lie",6],["scratch",0]],"en":"The doctor's voice was grave as she described the accident on the wet road. The damage to the small car was heavy, and one driver was close to death. She spoke gravely, without any hurry, and the family listened in silence. It was a serious moment, and no one dared to scratch a joke. Her accent told us she had come from another region, yet her words were clear. In the next room a young man lay on a bed, too weak to move. The gravity of his case would decide what the surgeons did next. Outside, the rain kept falling on the empty street.","zh":"医生描述湿滑路面上的那场车祸时，声音很沉重。那辆小轿车损毁得很重，一名司机已经濒临死亡。她说得很郑重，不慌不忙，一家人默默听着。那是个严肃的时刻，谁也不敢拿这事开玩笑。她的口音说明她来自别的地区，可话说得清楚。隔壁房间里，一个年轻人躺在床上，虚弱得动不了。他病情的严重程度，将决定外科医生接下来怎么做。外面，雨不停地下在空荡荡的街上。"},"dispose":{"tw":[["disposition",4],["qualify",0],["waste",3],["prepare",2],["liquidate",6],["toss",0],["dump",3],["sell",2],["procure",6],["discard",0]],"en":"When my uncle closed his old workshop, he had to dispose of years of tools. He would toss the broken ones into a box and dump the rest at the yard. Nothing was to be wasted without a thought, so he began to prepare a list. A dealer came to look at the good machines, hoping to procure a few and sell them on. My uncle had to qualify each item before he could set a price. His calm disposition helped when the dealer tried to bargain. In the end he chose to liquidate the whole workshop at once. He did not discard the small hammer his father had used; that came home with him.","zh":"我叔叔关掉他那间旧作坊时，得处理掉攒了多年的工具。破的他丢进一个箱子，其余的拉到废料场倒掉。什么都不该不加思索就浪费掉，于是他动手列了一份清单。一个贩子来看那些好机器，想收几台转手卖出去。每样东西他都得掂量过才敢定价。贩子想压价时，他那副沉稳的性情帮了忙。最后他决定把整个作坊一次清盘。父亲用过的那把小锤子他没舍得扔，带回了家。"},"drift":{"tw":[["drive",4],["blow",0],["stream",3],["change",2],["creep",6],["roll",0],["tide",3],["force",2],["slope",6],["cast",0]],"en":"On the third night at sea the wind began to blow softly, and our small boat started to drift. With no engine, we could only let the tide drive us slowly east. A cold stream of air came off the water and made everyone creep under a blanket. The boat would roll a little with each wave, and the sky began to change from black to grey. We watched the last stars fade on the long slope of the horizon. There was no force in our sail, only patience. In the morning I cast a rope to a passing boat and we were pulled home.","zh":"出海第三晚，风轻轻刮起来，我们那条小船开始漂。没有发动机，我们只能任由潮水推着慢慢往东。一股冷气从水面上涌来，让大家都缩到毯子底下。船随着每道浪微微摇晃，天色开始由黑转灰。我们看着最后几颗星星在地平线那道长长的斜线上淡下去。帆上没有半点力量，只有耐心。早上，我把一根绳子抛给一条路过的船，就这样被拖回了家。"},"entrance":{"tw":[["enter",4],["catch",0],["hold",3],["access",2],["gate",6],["charm",0],["work",3],["attract",2],["window",6],["capture",0]],"en":"The old theatre has one wide entrance and a small side gate. Visitors must enter through the front and show a ticket at the door. The manager says the building works hard to attract a young crowd, so the price stays low. A bright poster in the window is enough to catch the eye of anyone passing. Once inside, the charm of the red seats holds every guest for a whole evening. Cheap tickets give students easy access to good plays. A photographer came last week to capture the empty hall before the show. Later she sold the picture to a magazine for a fair price.","zh":"那座老剧院有一道宽阔的入口和一道小小的侧门。观众必须从前面进，在门口出示票。经理说，这栋房子很努力地想吸引年轻人，所以票价一直压得低。橱窗里一张鲜亮的海报，就足以让路过的任何人多看一眼。一进去，红色座椅的魅力能让每位客人坐上整晚。便宜的票让学生也能轻松看到好戏。上周一位摄影师赶来，在演出前拍下了空荡的大厅。后来她把照片卖给了一家杂志，价钱公道。"},"exclude":{"tw":[["exclusive",4],["except",0],["expel",2],["exorcise",3],["admit",1],["exclusion",4],["omit",0],["eject",0]],"en":"The old club liked to call itself exclusive, and its members would exclude anyone who did not pay the full fee. They would omit a name from the list for the smallest reason, expel a noisy guest, and even eject a member who arrived late. No one was admitted except the sons of old friends. That single rule kept the door half shut for years. Whole families felt the exclusion and stopped coming to the hall. A quiet teacher once said the club should exorcise such pride from its rules. The members only laughed. In the end, the empty chairs spoke louder than any speech.","zh":"那个老俱乐部爱自称排外，成员们会把任何不交全额会费的人排除在外。他们因为一点最小的理由就把名字从名单上删掉，把吵闹的客人赶出去，甚至把迟到的人驱逐出门。除了老朋友的儿子，谁都不许进。就这一条规矩，让那扇门关了好多年。整户整户的人尝过被排除的滋味，不再来会所了。一位沉默的老师曾说，这个俱乐部该把这种傲气从规矩里除掉。成员们只是笑。到头来，那些空椅子比任何讲话都说得更响。"},"generate":{"tw":[["generation",4],["father",0],["develop",3],["produce",2],["generator",4],["mother",0],["release",3],["return",0]],"en":"The old mill on the river has been in our family for three generations. My grandfather was the first to generate power from the falling water. He would tell my father how to develop a small machine that could produce enough light for one house. Later a bigger generator was built, and it would release a steady current all night. Each return of the spring flood meant a week of hard work. My mother kept the accounts and sold the extra power to a neighbour. Now I am learning to run the mill on my own. The river still turns the wheel, just as it did a hundred years ago.","zh":"河边那座老磨坊，在我们家已经传了三代。我祖父是头一个用水流落差发电的人。他常跟我父亲讲，怎么造一台小机器，能供一间屋子点灯。后来建了一台更大的发电机，整夜稳稳地送电。每逢春汛回来，就意味着一个星期的辛苦。我母亲管账，把多出来的电卖给邻居。如今我正学着自己打理这座磨坊。河水依然推着轮子转，就像一百年前那样。"},"imperial":{"tw":[["empire",4],["purple",0],["beard",2],["crown",6],["emperor",4],["royal",0],["queen",6],["regal",0]],"en":"In the museum there is a room about a great empire of the past. A grey stone bearded man stands at the door, and behind him hangs a heavy purple cloth. In the middle of the hall sits the crown of an emperor, thin and old. A guide explains that the imperial family once ruled from this very hill, and their royal banners hung from these walls. The queen in the painting has a calm, regal face and a long green dress. Scholars still argue about how the empire rose and fell. Children run past the glass cases without a glance. Yet the old power seems to fill the quiet room.","zh":"博物馆里有一间屋子，讲的是一片古代的大帝国。门口立着一个灰色石雕的络腮胡男子，他身后挂着一大幅厚重的紫布。大厅正中放着一位皇帝的冠冕，又薄又旧。讲解员说，这个皇室曾经就统治过脚下这座山丘，他们那些王家旗帜就挂在这些墙上。画里那位王后神情沉静，一副王者气度，穿着长长的绿裙。学者们至今还在争论这个帝国是怎样兴起又衰落的。孩子们从玻璃柜旁跑过，看都不看一眼。可那股古老的力量，似乎仍充满这间安静的屋子。"},"error":{"tw":[["err",4],["mistake",0],["slip",3],["failure",2],["difference",6],["fault",0],["blunder",3],["misconception",2],["result",6]],"en":"A single error in the lab book cost us two weeks of work. The mistake began as a small slip: I wrote one figure in the wrong line. It was my own fault, and I had to err on the side of honesty and tell the manager at once. A common misconception is that such a slip has no result. In truth the failure of the whole test came from that one number. The difference between success and waste was a single digit. The manager called it a costly blunder, but he did not shout. We repeated the test the next day, more carefully.","zh":"实验记录上单单一个错误，就让我们赔上两个星期的活。那错起初只是个小疏漏：我把一个数字写错了行。这是我自己的过失，我只能老老实实地马上告诉经理。一个常见的误解是，这样的疏漏不会有什么结果。事实上，整个试验的失败就出在那一个数字上。成与废的差别，只是一位数。经理说这算得上一次代价不小的失误，可他没吼。第二天，我们更仔细地把试验重做了一遍。"},"extension":{"tw":[["extend",4],["wing",0],["spread",3],["dance",2],["expansion",6],["annex",0],["stretch",3],["telephone",2],["option",6]],"en":"The school had to extend its old hall before the new term began. The plan for the expansion included a small annex at the back and a wide staircase. Builders would spread the work over three months, so the noise did not stop the classes. A new wing held two more rooms and a place for the dance club. The head teacher asked for one more telephone line as an option. Workers had to stretch a long cable from the gate to the office. In the end the extension was finished just in time. On the first morning the children ran down the new hall, laughing.","zh":"新学期开始前，学校得把旧礼堂扩建一下。扩建的方案里包括后面一个小附楼和一道宽楼梯。施工方把活儿分摊到三个月里，这样噪音就没耽误上课。新加的一翼多了两间房，还有一个给舞蹈社的地方。校长又申请加装一条电话线，当作备选。工人们得从大门口拉一根长电缆到办公室。最后，扩建总算赶在开学前完工。头一个早上，孩子们笑着跑过新礼堂。"},"gang":{"tw":[["gangster",4],["pack",0],["detail",3],["tool",2],["criminal",6],["ring",0],["nest",3],["unit",2],["crowd",0]],"en":"Last spring the police broke up a gang that had robbed three shops. One gangster gave the others away, and the whole criminal ring fell apart. Officers followed every detail of the case, from the tools they used to the cars they drove. A small unit stayed on the street for two nights, watching a quiet house. In its cellar they found a nest of stolen goods and a pack of false papers. A crowd gathered outside when the arrests were made. The leader had once worked in a shop, and the thefts were his way of paying old debts. The case was closed by summer.","zh":"去年春天，警方打掉了一个抢劫过三家商铺的团伙。一名歹徒供出了同伙，整个犯罪圈子就崩了。警员把这案子的每个细节都摸了一遍，从他们用的工具到开的车。一个小分队在街上蹲了两晚，盯着那栋安静的屋子。地窖里发现了一窝赃物和一沓假证件。抓人的时候，外面围了一群人。头目从前在一家店里干过活，这些偷盗不过是他还旧债的手段。案子到夏天就结了。"},"impression":{"tw":[["impress",4],["picture",0],["mark",3],["idea",2],["sense",6],["effect",3],["image",3],["press",2],["opinion",0]],"en":"On my first day at the old print shop I wanted to make a good impression. The manager showed me a heavy press and asked me to mark every page in the same corner. He had a clear idea of how the work should look, and his opinion was respected by everyone. A pressed image must sit straight, he said, or the whole picture feels wrong. I soon found that a small mark can have a large effect on the eye. My first sheet was not perfect, and the sense of shame was strong. But no one laughed. By the end of the week I could impress even the oldest worker.","zh":"在老印刷铺上班的头一天，我想给人留个好印象。经理让我看一台沉甸甸的印刷机，要我把每一页都在同一个角落做个记号。他心里很清楚地知道活儿该是什么样，他的意见大家都很看重。他说，印出来的图必须摆正，否则整张画面就觉得别扭。我很快发现，一个小小的记号也能对眼睛产生很大的影响。我印出的头一张并不完美，那种羞愧感很强。可是没人笑我。到那个星期末，我连最老的师傅都能让他另眼相看。"},"delay":{"tw":[["check",2],["break",3],["change",2],["rush",1],["postpone",6],["hold",0],["catch",3],["pause",2],["possible",6],["stay",3]],"en":"A heavy snow caused a long delay on our morning train. The staff had to check the rails before they would let us go. There was a sudden break in the signal, and the driver had to hold the train at the last station. The company chose to postpone two later trips, which caused a rush of angry calls. We could not change our seats, so we had to stay where we were. After a short pause the speaker said the line was clear again. It was, they said, as fast as possible. We finally caught the evening bus into town, hours late.","zh":"一场大雪让我们早上那趟火车晚点很久。工作人员得先检查铁轨，才肯放我们走。信号突然断了一下，司机只好把车停在上一站。铁路公司决定推迟后面两趟车，惹得电话一片抱怨。我们没法换座位，只能待在原地。停了一小会儿，广播说线路又通了。他们说，这已经是最快的了。我们最后搭上了傍晚那班进城的公交，晚了几个钟头。"},"differ":{"tw":[["difference",4],["disagree",0],["contrast",3],["equal",1],["correspond",6],["different",4],["reflect",6]],"en":"Two reports about the accident differ in almost every line. The first says the road was wet; the second says it was dry, and the two accounts disagree on the time as well. By contrast, they agree on one thing: no one was badly hurt. The figures in each report are not equal and do not correspond at all. One paper gives a total of forty, the other a number that seems to reflect a different count. The difference is small but real, and a careful reader will see it. No two witnesses see the same event, the police said. Both stories may be honest, and both may be partly true.","zh":"关于那场事故的两份报告，几乎每一行都不一样。第一份说路面是湿的；第二份说是干的，两份对时间也说法不一。相比之下，它们在一件事上是一致的：没有人受重伤。两份报告里的数字根本对不上。一份报纸给出总数四十，另一份的数字似乎映出的是另一种数法。这点差别不大，却是实实在在的，细心的读者看得出来。警方说，没有两个目击者看到的是同一件事。两种说法也许都诚实，也许多少都对。"},"discharge":{"tw":[["clear",3],["blow",3],["flow",2],["charge",1],["maximum",6],["complete",0],["cut",3],["material",2],["ballast",6],["drop",0]],"en":"Last year the factory had to stop the way it would discharge its waste water into the river. The flow had once been heavy enough to turn the water grey, and the charge for the cleanup was high. Engineers set a maximum for what the plant could release, and they had to cut the amount by half. To complete the work they used new material that would clear the water faster. A large tank of ballast was moved to steady the pipe, and the old pumps began to blow hot air. In the end the council ordered them to drop the old practice for good. The river is cleaner now, and fish have come back.","zh":"去年，这家工厂不得不停止往河里排放废水的老做法。以往那股水流大得能把河水变成灰色，清理的费用也很高。工程师给厂里定了排放的最高限度，得把量砍掉一半。为了把工程做完，他们用了能让水更快变清的新材料。一只装满压舱物的大罐被移来稳住管道，旧水泵开始往外吐热气。最后，市政会命令他们彻底放弃老办法。如今河水干净多了，鱼也回来了。"},"disorder":{"tw":[["trouble",0],["mess",3],["change",2],["order",1],["chronic",6],["upset",0],["worry",3],["state",2],["mental",6],["distract",0]],"en":"After the move, our new flat fell into complete disorder. Boxes lay in a mess on the floor, and the change of address had upset everyone a little. My brother, who suffers from a chronic illness, found the noise hard to bear. In such a state it was easy to worry and to let small problems distract us. We agreed to bring back order one room at a time. His doctor said that a calm home helps the mental health as much as any pill. So we worked slowly, without blame. By the second week the trouble was gone, and the flat felt like ours.","zh":"搬完家，我们的新公寓一片混乱。箱子乱七八糟摊在地上，换了地址也让每个人有点心烦。我弟弟有慢性病，那些噪音他实在受不了。在这种状态下，人很容易发愁，也容易被小事分了心。我们说好一间屋子一间屋子地把秩序收回来。医生说，一个安稳的家对心理健康的帮助，不亚于任何药片。于是我们慢慢收拾，谁也不怪谁。到第二周，麻烦没了，公寓也真像是我们的家了。"},"dominant":{"tw":[["dominate",4],["predominant",0],["note",2],["subordinate",1],["distinct",6],["dominance",4],["strong",6]],"en":"In the debate club one strong voice would dominate the room. Her dominance was clear, yet she never spoke over others. A single note in her voice was her dominant weapon; it was the predominant sound in every round. The other speakers stayed subordinate and waited their turn. Each idea she gave was distinct, and no one could confuse it with another. Even so, a quiet boy would one day challenge her. The older members smiled, because they saw a second strong mind arrive. That was when the club truly began to grow.","zh":"辩论社里，有一个强劲的声音主导着全场。她的优势很明显，可她从不抢别人的话。她嗓音里那一个音调就是她最厉害的武器；每一轮里，那都是最占上风的声音。其他发言的人都处在从属的位置，等着轮到自己。她给出的每个看法都各有分别，谁也不会同别的搞混。即便如此，一个沉默的男孩总有一天会来挑战她。老成员们笑了，因为他们看到又一颗强韧的头脑来了。也就是从那时起，这个社才真正开始壮大。"},"element":{"tw":[["elementary",4],["component",0],["environment",2],["dimension",6],["elemental",4],["factor",0],["ingredient",0]],"en":"The teacher held up a small pot and asked what the most important element of a healthy garden was. Water, said one child; soil, said another. She told them that light is a key component, and that the environment matters as much as any single factor. Even an elementary idea can have a hidden dimension, she said. A good soil is an ingredient in everything that grows, and it holds a little of each elemental thing: air, water, and stone. The class then planted seeds in a box by the window. By spring each child had a small green plant.","zh":"老师举起一只小花盆，问一座健康的园子里最重要的要素是什么。一个孩子说水；另一个说是土。她告诉他们，光是一个关键的组成部分，环境的重要程度不亚于任何一个单独的因素。她说，哪怕一个最基本的想法，也可能藏着意想不到的一面。好土是一切生长的成分，它里头含着每一种最基本的物质：空气、水，还有石头。接着全班在窗边的箱子里种下了种子。到春天，每个孩子都有了一株小小的绿苗。"},"function":{"tw":[["office",0],["cut",3],["duty",2],["malfunction",1],["integral",6],["run",0],["double",3],["software",2],["specific",6],["serve",2]],"en":"Every machine in the office has one function, and the printer's job is to serve the whole floor. When a small malfunction appeared, the manager's first duty was to call for help. He had to run a test on the software and check every specific setting. A loose part was the cause, and a quick cut of the power fixed it. The technician said the printer was integral to the daily work, and that a double check would save trouble later. It must work in any office, in sun or shade. By noon the pages were moving again. Nobody thanked the machine, but everyone was glad.","zh":"办公室里的每台机器都有一样功能，那台打印机的职责就是为整个楼层服务。出了一点小故障，经理首先该做的就是喊人来修。他得给软件跑一遍测试，检查每一项具体的设置。病根是一个松掉的零件，很快地断一下电就修好了。技师说，这台打印机是日常工作的必需，多查一遍能省去以后的麻烦。它得在任何一个办公室里都能用，不管日晒还是阴凉。到中午，纸又重新走起来了。没人谢那台机器，可人人都松了口气。"},"import":{"tw":[["moment",0],["matter",3],["mean",2],["export",1],["tariff",6],["spell",0],["sense",3],["message",2],["grain",6],["consequence",0]],"en":"An old trader once explained the import of a new tariff on grain. For him the whole matter was simple: a tax on what you buy is always a question of great moment for a small shop. Long ago he would export flour to a town across the water, and the profit helped him through a hard spell. Now he reads the message on every bill and tries to find its true sense. What does the change mean for a family like his? No one can yet say what the consequence will be. He keeps his accounts in a careful hand. A quiet man, he says little, but he sees a lot.","zh":"一位老商人曾讲过新的粮食关税意味着什么。对他来说，整件事很简单：对买进的东西征税，对小店来说永远是一件极要紧的事。很久以前，他会把面粉出口到对岸的一个镇子，那点利润帮他熬过了一段艰难的日子。如今他读每一张单据上的信息，想弄懂它真正的意思。这样的变化对他这样的家庭意味着什么？会有什么后果，谁也还说不准。他把账记在一手工整的小字里。他是个话不多的人，可看得很透。"},"division":{"tw":[["divide",4],["class",0],["cut",3],["unit",6],["section",0],["game",3],["corps",6],["partition",0]],"en":"Last year the firm split its biggest division into three parts. The head had to divide the work so that each unit could stand alone. One section took the shops, another the farms, and a third the small repair corps. A thin partition came down between two offices, and a glass door was cut in the wall. In the first game of the year the two new teams played against each other and laughed. A class of young workers was hired to learn the whole system. It was not easy, but the change was fair. By summer each part was making its own small profit.","zh":"去年，公司把它最大的一个部门拆成了三块。负责人得把活儿分开，好让每个单元都能独立运转。一个科管店铺，另一个管农庄，第三个管那支小小的维修队。两间办公室之间竖起一道薄隔板，墙上开出一扇玻璃门。那年头一场球赛里，两支新队伍对着打，笑成一团。还招了一批年轻工人来学整套流程。这不容易，可这次变动是公道的。到夏天，每一块都在自己赚一点小钱了。"},"entry":{"tw":[["enter",4],["entrance",0],["credit",3],["access",2],["allow",6],["admission",3],["message",2],["status",6]],"en":"Each night my grandmother would write one short entry in her diary. The first line always held the date, and the rest was a simple message about her day. She did not allow anyone to read it while she lived, and there was no admission that it even existed. To enter the room where she kept it, you had to pass a narrow entrance near the kitchen. Years later I was given access to the whole book. Some pages carried small credit for the friends who had helped her. Reading them, I felt a quiet change in my own status in the family. She had kept a record none of us knew about.","zh":"每天晚上，我奶奶都会在日记里写一小段。头一行总是日期，其余的是关于她这一天的一句简单留言。她活着时不许任何人看，也从没承认过有这本日记。要进她收着日记的那间屋子，得走过厨房旁边一道窄窄的入口。多年以后，我才获准看整本日记。有些页上，还替帮过她的朋友记着一份小小的功劳。读着读着，我感觉到自己在家里的位置悄悄变了。她留下的这份记录，我们谁都不知道。"},"exclusive":{"tw":[["exclude",4],["single",0],["report",2],["inclusive",1],["access",6],["sole",0],["status",6],["scoop",0]],"en":"The young reporter wanted one exclusive story before the year ended. Her editor told her that a single strong report could change everything. The club she wrote about was proud and closed; it would exclude any outsider from its rooms. Only a member had access to the inner hall, and the sole way in was a back door. The old owner loved his high status and never spoke to the press. Yet she got her scoop when a member left the club and spoke to her. The story was inclusive of every voice, even the owner's. It changed how the town saw that place.","zh":"那位年轻记者想在年底前弄到一篇独家报道。编辑告诉她，一篇有分量的报道就能改变一切。她写到的那个俱乐部又骄傲又闭塞，任何外人都被挡在门外。只有会员才能进到里面的大厅，唯一的通路是一扇后门。老老板爱惜自己高高在上的身份，从不跟媒体讲话。可她还是抢到了独家新闻：一位会员退出了俱乐部，开口对她讲了。这篇报道容下了每一个声音，连老板的也在内。它改变了全镇对那个地方的看法。"},"decline":{"tw":[["fall",0],["slip",3],["condition",2],["rise",6],["correct",0],["bounce",3],["decrease",2],["trend",6],["refuse",0]],"en":"Sales of the old phone began to decline after the new model came out. The numbers would fall every month, and the trend was clear. The company could not correct the problem fast enough. They saw a decrease in almost every market. Meanwhile the price of parts began to rise. One small slip in the design was enough to change the whole picture. The old phone would refuse to work with the new software, so the buyers walked away. The firm had to bounce back with a cheaper model. The condition of the market was hard that year.","zh":"新机型一上市，这款旧手机的销量就开始下滑。数字每个月都在跌，趋势一目了然。公司来不及纠正这个问题。几乎每个市场都出现了减少。与此同时，零件价格开始上涨。设计上一点小闪失就足以改变整个局面。旧手机不肯兼容新软件，买家便转身走了。公司只好靠一款更便宜的机型重新振作。那一年的市场行情很难。"},"decrease":{"tw":[["fall",0],["break",3],["change",2],["increase",1],["rate",6],["diminish",0],["cut",3],["process",2],["decline",6]],"en":"Last year the number of wild birds began to decrease along the river. The rate of the fall worried every farmer. A slow change in the water could diminish the fish as well. The council decided to cut the waste from the old factory. As the process went on, the birds started to return. There was even a small increase in spring. The decline had not been endless after all. My teacher said one broken link can make a whole system fail. The lesson was simple: small steps can save a place.","zh":"去年，河边的野鸟数量开始减少。下降的速度让每个农民都担心。水质慢慢变化，鱼也会跟着变少。议会决定削减那家老厂的排污。随着这一过程推进，鸟儿开始回来了。春天甚至有了一点回升。这场衰退终究不是没有尽头的。老师说，一个断掉的环节就能让整个系统失灵。道理很简单：小小的举措也能救回一个地方。"},"defeat":{"tw":[["kill",0],["beat",3],["failure",2],["victory",1],["win",6],["overcome",0],["nose",3],["veto",2],["triumph",6]],"en":"Our team had to face one hard defeat in the final match. Nobody liked the taste of failure, but we had to accept it. The other side would beat us by a single goal. One missed pass can kill a team's hope in a second. Two players tried to find a nose for the goal, but the keeper was too good. We had no chance to win, and no victory to celebrate. The coach said we should overcome our pride and learn from it. The judge had to veto a late point, which hurt. Still, in that small triumph of effort, we felt proud.","zh":"决赛里，我们队不得不面对一场难受的败仗。没人喜欢失败的味道，可我们得接受它。对方以一个球的优势赢了我们。一次传丢，就能一瞬间掐灭一支球队的希望。两名队员想找准球门的感觉，可守门员太稳了。我们没有机会赢，也没有胜利可庆祝。教练说，我们该放下傲气，从中吸取教训。裁判还否决了最后一分，让人心里发堵。可即便这样，在那点努力换来的小小成就里，我们还是感到骄傲。"},"demonstrate":{"tw":[["present",0],["reflect",3],["protest",2],["regard",6],["establish",0],["picket",3],["confirm",2],["recognize",6],["evidence",0]],"en":"In the science class we had to demonstrate how water moves through sand. Our teacher would present a simple glass box and a small bottle. We had to reflect the light so the lines could be seen. Two students used a thin stick to establish a clear path. The result helped confirm our idea and even gave us better evidence. Later, outside, some workers began to picket the gate in protest against a new road. People stopped to watch with little regard for the rain. It was a good day to recognize how small tests can explain big things.","zh":"科学课上，我们要演示水是怎样穿过沙子的。老师拿出一只简单的玻璃箱和一个小瓶。我们得把光反上去，才能看清那些线。两个同学用一根细棍子理出一条清晰的路线。结果印证了我们的想法，还给了我们更好的证据。后来在外面，一些工人开始在大门口举牌抗议修新路。人们停下来看，顾不上淋雨。这一天让我明白，小小的试验也能解释大事。"},"derive":{"tw":[["gain",0],["reap",3],["reason",2],["attribute",6],["descend",0],["surmise",3],["evolve",2],["translate",6],["infer",0]],"en":"Many words in our language derive from older roots. A student can gain a lot by learning where each one came from. From a single old word, a hundred new ones may descend and slowly evolve. We can translate a line and then surmise its first meaning. My teacher would reason with us and ask what we could infer from the shape of the word. She said we should not attribute every change to chance. In the end we could reap the reward of a better memory. It was a quiet lesson, but a useful one.","zh":"我们语言里的许多词都源自更古老的字根。学生弄懂每个词的来历，能收获很多。从一个古词里，可能派生出上百个新词，再慢慢演变。我们可以把一句翻出来，再猜它最初的意思。老师会跟我们讲道理，问我们从这个词的形态上能推出什么。她说，不要把所有变化都归因于偶然。最后我们收获了更好的记性。这是一堂安静的课，却很有用。"},"designate":{"tw":[["indicate",0],["finger",3],["inform",2],["prime",6],["assign",0],["mean",3],["plan",2],["minister",6],["delegate",0]],"en":"At the meeting the head had to designate one room for the new office. She would indicate the corner with a long finger and mark it on the map. Her plan was to assign two clerks there and delegate the daily work to a young man. She asked us to inform the minister of the small church nearby before Friday. The word 'prime' would mean the best spot in the whole building. Everyone agreed it was a good choice. Later a small red sign would designate the door itself. The office was ready by noon.","zh":"会上，负责人得指定一间屋子做新办公室。她用一根长手指点出那个角落，在地图上标下来。她打算派两名职员到那儿，把日常事务交给一个年轻人。她让我们在周五之前通知附近那小教堂的牧师。'prime'这个词指的是整栋楼里最好的位置。大家都同意这是个好选择。后来门上挂了一块小红色标牌。到中午，办公室就收拾好了。"},"discount":{"tw":[["dismiss",0],["allow",3],["decrease",2],["retail",6],["disregard",0],["slight",3],["reject",2],["price",6],["rebate",3]],"en":"The retail shop would allow a small discount on every winter coat. The owner said he could not dismiss the rising costs, so the decrease in price was slight. He would reject any offer below the marked number. A quiet rebate at the door helped the poorer buyers. Some customers would disregard the sign and ask for more. He could only shake his head and point to the price. In the end the shop sold most of its stock. A fair deal, he said, is better than a big one.","zh":"这家零售店给每件冬外套都让一点折扣。老板说，不断上涨的成本他不能不顾，所以降价的幅度很小。低于标价的出价，他一概拒绝。门口还悄悄给一笔回扣，帮了手头紧的顾客。有些客人不理那块牌子，还想再要。他只能摇摇头，指指标价。最后店里卖掉了大部分存货。他说，公道的买卖比大买卖更值。"},"dismiss":{"tw":[["drop",0],["slight",3],["change",2],["decision",6],["fire",0],["retire",3],["remove",2],["appeal",6],["ignore",0]],"en":"The manager had to dismiss a young worker for a serious mistake. It was not a quick decision, and he did not treat it as a slight matter. The man had let a drop of oil fall on the new machine and then tried to ignore the fault. The company could not change the rule for him. They had to remove his name from the list and ask him to retire early. He would make one appeal to the office, but it was refused. Later they had to fire a second worker as well. It was a hard week for the whole team.","zh":"因为一个严重失误，经理不得不开除一名年轻工人。这不是个轻易的决定，他也没把它当成小事。那人让一滴油落在新机器上，还想瞒着不报。公司不能为他改规矩。他们只好把名字从名单上划掉，让他提前退休。他向办公室申诉了一次，被驳回了。后来他们又不得不辞掉了第二个工人。对整个班组来说，这是难熬的一周。"},"dispute":{"tw":[["challenge",0],["call",3],["argue",2],["issue",6],["conflict",0],["controversy",3],["contest",2],["resolve",6],["scrap",0]],"en":"A long dispute between two shops began over a shared wall. Each side would argue that the space was theirs. The owner would call the other and challenge him to show the old plan. The real issue was who should pay for repairs. The conflict grew into a public controversy that filled the local paper. They even entered a small contest about the sign. For two years neither shop would give in. In the end a kind neighbour helped them resolve the quarrel, and they tore up the old scrap of paper and shook hands.","zh":"两家店铺为共用的一堵墙起了长期的争执。双方都辩称那块地方是自己的。一位店主打电话给另一位，要他把旧图纸拿出来比。真正的问题在于谁该出修墙的钱。这场冲突闹成了一场风波，本地的报纸都登了。他们甚至还为那块招牌打了个小官司。最后一位好心的邻居帮他们化解了这场争吵。他们撕掉那页旧纸，握了握手。"},"draft":{"tw":[["outline",0],["check",3],["drink",2],["review",6],["enlist",0],["recruit",3],["pull",2],["sign",6],["blueprint",0]],"en":"My editor asked me to write a first draft of the report before noon. I began with a short outline and a rough blueprint of the main points. She would check each line and then review the whole page with me. We had to pull two old charts from the file. She asked me to sign the paper only after her final review. A young writer came to enlist our help with a school paper. The office hoped to recruit one more hand for the week. I took a long drink of water and began again.","zh":"编辑让我中午之前把报告的第一稿写出来。我先写了一份简短的提纲和一张要点草图。她会逐行检查，再和我一起通看整页。我们得从档案里抽出两张旧图表。她让我等最后审完再签字。一个年轻作者来请我们帮他做校报。办公室想再招一个人来干这一周。我喝了一大口水，又接着写。"},"elaborate":{"tw":[["complicate",0],["detail",3],["change",2],["intricate",6],["expand",0],["specify",3],["produce",2],["formal",6],["enlarge",0]],"en":"The engineer gave an elaborate account of how the new pump works. He would specify each part in careful detail and then expand on the main idea. The design was intricate, and a small change could complicate the whole system. He had to produce a formal report for the office. On the last page a large drawing would enlarge one small ring. My uncle, who had built pumps for years, asked him to simplify. The young man smiled and said he would try. It was a long but useful talk.","zh":"这位工程师详细地讲了新水泵是怎么运转的。他把每个零件都仔细说明，再展开讲主要原理。设计很繁复，一处小小的改动就可能把整个系统弄复杂。他得给办公室交一份正式报告。最后一页上有一张大图，把一个小圆环放大。我叔叔做了多年水泵，让他讲简单点。年轻人笑了笑，说他会试试。这场谈话很长，却很有用。"},"embrace":{"tw":[["cover",0],["clinch",3],["accept",2],["desire",6],["adopt",0],["cuddle",3],["include",2],["inspire",6],["squeeze",0]],"en":"When my brother came home after a long year away, my mother ran to embrace him. She would cuddle him like a small child and cover his face with kisses. My father gave a firm hand to clinch the greeting. It was easy to accept how much the family had missed him. His own desire was simple: a warm meal and a quiet night. The family decided to adopt one new habit, a slow walk after dinner together. The old house would include his room, still ready for him, and his stories would inspire my little sister. He had to squeeze past two boxes to reach the door.","zh":"哥哥在外头待了整整一年，一回家，母亲就扑上去抱他。她像抱小孩一样搂着他，在他脸上亲个不停。父亲紧紧握了下手，把这份问候定了下来。我们很自然地接受了：全家都那么想他。他自己的心愿很简单：一顿热饭，一个安静的夜。一家人决定养成一个新习惯，晚饭后一起慢慢散步。老房子会给他留着房间，一直备着；他的见闻也让小妹妹心生向往。他得从两个箱子中间挤过去才能进门。"},"endure":{"tw":[["bear",0],["accept",3],["continue",2],["suffer",6],["last",2],["die",3],["experience",2],["torment",6],["live",0]],"en":"For two long months my grandfather had to endure the pain in his knee. He would bear it with a quiet face and never complain. The doctor said the damage could last for years if he did not rest. He had to accept the slow work of healing and continue his simple exercises each day. He did not want to suffer in silence for nothing, and he would not let his hope die. My grandmother said the experience had changed him. He would live for the morning walks again. The torment of waiting was the hardest part of all.","zh":"整整两个月，爷爷都得忍着膝盖的疼。他一声不吭地扛着，从不抱怨。医生说，要是不好好休息，这伤能拖上好几年。他得接受康复的慢功夫，每天接着做那几样简单的练习。他不想白白默默受苦，也不肯让希望熄灭。奶奶说，这一遭把他人也变了。他又能为早上的散步而活了。等待的煎熬才是最难的。"},"essay":{"tw":[["test",0],["control",3],["act",2],["preface",6],["try",0],["fight",3],["evaluate",2],["book",6],["attempt",2]],"en":"Before the test my sister had to write a long essay about her home town. She would try to control her fear of the blank page. The first attempt was weak, so she wrote a short preface and began again. In the middle she had to fight the wish to give up. Her teacher would evaluate each line with a red pen. She read an old book for a better opening line. It was her first real act as a young writer. In the end the essay filled three pages, and she was proud.","zh":"考试之前，妹妹得写一篇关于家乡的长作文。她会努力压住面对空白纸张的紧张。第一次尝试写得很弱，于是她写了个小引言，重新写过。写到一半，她还得跟想放弃的念头较劲。老师会用红笔逐行讲评。她读了一本旧书，想找个更好的开头。这是她第一次真正当个小作者。最后这篇作文写满了三页，她很自豪。"},"exceed":{"tw":[["pass",0],["better",3],["beat",2],["limit",6],["top",0],["shame",3],["excel",2],["minimum",6],["transcend",0]],"en":"The little car could not exceed the speed limit on the hill road. My uncle said a better driver might pass the truck ahead. He did not want to beat the clock or top any record. He kept both hands on the wheel and his eyes on the wet road. One sharp turn could shame us all. His aim was to excel at safety, not speed. The engine could transcend its small size only on a dry day. We stopped for water at the minimum stop, then went on. It was a long road, but a safe one.","zh":"那辆小车在山路上超不过限速。叔叔说换个更好的司机也许能超过前面那辆卡车。他不想抢时间，也不想创什么纪录。一个急转弯就够让所有人丢脸了。他要的是在安全上拔尖，而不是比快。只有在干燥的日子，这台发动机才能超出它的小个头。我们在最低限度的一次停靠喝了点水，又往前赶。路很长，却走得安稳。"},"fate":{"tw":[["lot",0],["doom",3],["condition",2],["doubt",6],["luck",0],["misfortune",3],["ordain",2],["whether",6],["fortune",0]],"en":"The old fisherman often talked about fate and luck. He would doubt that anyone could change the condition of the sea. In his long life he had known both good fortune and deep misfortune. He said no one could ordain the hour of the storm. Whether the boat came home was never certain. His lot, he believed, was to work and wait. Still, he would not give in to doom. In the end the women on the shore, not fate, kept the families safe. He told that story every winter.","zh":"那位老渔夫常说起命运和运气。他不大相信有人能改变海上的境况。一辈子下来，他既见过好福气，也遭过大不幸。他说，谁也定不了暴风雨到来的时辰。船能不能回家，从来说不准。他相信，自己的命份就是干活和等待。可他也不肯向厄运低头。到头来，让一个个家庭平安的，是岸上的女人们，不是命运。这个故事他每年冬天都讲。"},"filter":{"tw":[["strain",0],["infiltrate",3],["run",2],["sensor",6],["trickle",0],["leach",3],["separate",2],["packet",6],["dribble",0]],"en":"The new filter on the pipe removes fine dust from the water. It can strain even the smallest grains and separate them from the clear part. A sensor inside will warn us when the mesh is full. Dirty water may trickle through and then run into the tank below. Salt from the road can leach into the soil and infiltrate the old well. I had to change the packet inside twice a month. A slow dribble from a loose joint showed the fault. The repair was small, but the air in the room felt cleaner.","zh":"水管上的新滤器能把水里的细尘滤掉。它连最小的颗粒都能筛住，把它们和清水分开。里面的一个传感器会在滤网满了时提醒我们。脏水可能慢慢渗过来，再流进下面那个水箱。路上的盐会渗进土里，再渗入老井。我得每个月换一次里面的滤芯。接头处一滴一滴地漏，露出了毛病。修理不大，可屋里的空气清爽了许多。"},"flavour":{"tw":[["feel",0],["charm",3],["taste",2],["aroma",6],["look",0],["salt",3],["atmosphere",2],["blend",6],["smell",0]],"en":"My grandmother would blend a few simple spices to give the soup a deep flavour. The aroma would fill the whole kitchen and make everyone feel warm. A single grain of salt could change the taste. She liked the old charm of her iron pot, though it looked worn. She would smell the steam and nod. She said the atmosphere of a meal is half the pleasure. We had to taste it twice before she was happy. The kitchen smelled of warm bread and onions all afternoon. Then she let us sit and eat.","zh":"奶奶会把几样简单的香料调在一起，给汤添上一股浓味。那股香气充满整间厨房，让每个人心里都暖。一粒盐就能改变味道。她喜欢那只旧铁锅的韵味，虽然它看着旧了。她会闻闻蒸汽，点点头。她说，一顿饭的气氛占了一半的乐趣。我们得尝两遍，她才满意。然后她才让我们坐下吃。"},"formula":{"tw":[["normal",0],["primitive",3],["direction",2],["model",6],["rule",0],["algorithm",3],["procedure",2],["race",6],["pattern",0]],"en":"The young engineer wrote a simple formula on the board to find the fastest way home. It was no normal rule, but a small algorithm for the bus. She would model each turn on paper and give the whole procedure a name. The pattern of stops formed a clear direction for the driver. The first tool her class used was a primitive one: a pen and a map. They would race two routes to see which was quicker. In the end the old formula worked, and everyone clapped. Simple rules, she said, often win.","zh":"年轻的工程师在黑板上写下一个简单的公式，用来找出回家最快的路。这不是什么寻常的规律，而是一套给公交用的小算法。她会在纸上把每个转弯都建模，再给整套流程起个名。站点的分布给司机指出了一个清楚的方向。她们班最早用的工具很原始：一支笔和一张地图。他们会把两条路线拿来赛一赛，看哪条更快。最后那条老公式奏效了，大家都拍手。她说，简单的规则常常能赢。"},"gap":{"tw":[["break",0],["hole",3],["open",2],["spur",6],["crack",3],["mouth",3],["pass",2],["balance",6],["spread",0]],"en":"One long winter left a wide gap in the old stone wall. A crack had grown into a hole, and the cold wind could pass right through. My uncle had to break away the loose stones and open the gap a little wider. He put a small spur of wood across it to keep the shape. Then he had to balance two heavy blocks on top. The mouth of the gap was soon closed with new mortar. He said the spread of frost had done the damage. We finished before the next snow.","zh":"一个漫长的冬天在那堵老石墙上留下了一道宽缝。一条裂缝变成个洞，冷风能直接穿过去。叔叔只好把松动的石头拆掉，把缺口再开大一点。他横着支了一小段木头，把形状撑住。然后他得在顶上把两块重石摆平。缺口的口子很快就用新灰浆封上了。他说，是霜的蔓延弄坏了它。赶在下一场雪前，我们干完了。"},"glow":{"tw":[["burn",0],["flush",3],["feel",2],["luminous",6],["shine",2],["gutter",3],["light",2],["faint",6],["beam",0]],"en":"At dusk a soft glow filled the small room from the old lamp. The bulb would burn low and give a faint light on the wall. I could feel the warmth on my face and see a flush on my sister's cheeks. The lamp near the gutter of the window would shine like a small star. It looked almost luminous in the dark. A thin beam from a passing car crossed the floor and was gone. Then the room grew quiet again. Nothing else moved in the whole house that night. I liked that calm hour best.","zh":"黄昏时，一盏旧灯把柔柔的辉光洒满小屋。灯泡烧得低低的，在墙上投下微弱的光。我能感到脸上的暖意，也看见妹妹两颊泛红。窗槽边那盏灯亮得像颗小星星。在暗处它几乎泛着光。一道细光从一辆过路的车上扫过地板，转眼没了。屋子又静下来。我最喜欢这个安静的时刻。"},"grain":{"tw":[["texture",0],["rice",3],["form",2],["export",6],["cereal",0],["corn",3],["paint",2],["maize",6],["granulate",0]],"en":"On the long table my mother spread a sack of grain from the last harvest. She would form a small hill of rice and corn beside it. The texture of each kind was different under the hand. A big farm nearby would export a part of its cereal to other towns. My father liked to eat warm maize with salt. He showed me how the mill could granulate the seeds into powder. A little water turned the powder into paint for the barn. The sack was heavy, and the work left our hands dusty. It was a slow, honest morning.","zh":"长桌上，母亲摊开上一季收的一袋谷子。她会把大米和玉米在旁边拢成一小堆。每一种在手底下的质地都不一样。附近一个大农场会把一部分谷物出口到别的镇上。父亲爱吃撒了盐的热玉米。他给我演示磨盘怎样把种子磨成粉。加点水，粉就调成了刷谷仓的涂料。这是个慢悠悠、踏实的上午。"},"grasp":{"tw":[["dig",0],["figure",3],["understand",2],["comprehend",6],["hold",2],["sense",3],["influence",2],["perspective",6],["reach",0]],"en":"The teacher tried to help us grasp a hard idea about the stars. She would dig into the old books to find a simple figure for the class. It was not easy to understand at first, and few could comprehend it whole. She asked us to hold one idea in mind and give it our own sense. Her quiet influence made even the shy students reach for an answer. She wanted us to see the sky from a new perspective. By the end of the hour most of us had it. Knowledge, she said, grows slowly.","zh":"老师想帮我们领会一个关于星星的难懂道理。她会钻进旧书里，给全班找一个简单的图形。这道理一开始不好懂，没几个人能整个弄明白。她让我们把一个念头记在心上，再用自己的感觉去理解。她那份安静的影响，让连害羞的学生也伸手去够答案。她想让我们从新的角度看天空。到下课的时候，我们大多都懂了。她说，知识长得慢。"},"grip":{"tw":[["bag",0],["bite",3],["interest",2],["heel",6],["handle",0],["stock",3],["influence",2],["dominance",6],["hold",0]],"en":"The old farmer would grip the handle of his tool and never let go. His strong grip came from years of work in the field. He kept his whole stock of seeds in a leather bag by the door. The thin heel of his boot had worn down on the hard ground. He had a real interest in every kind of grain. Once a small dog tried to bite his hand, but he kept his hold. His quiet influence over the young workers was strong, yet he never wanted dominance. He said good work speaks for itself.","zh":"老农会紧紧握住工具的柄，从不撒手。他这手劲是常年在田里干活练出来的。他把全部的种子都存在门边一只皮包里。他靴子的薄后跟被硬地磨平了。他对每一种谷物都有真兴趣。有一次一只小狗想咬他的手，他也没松开。他对年轻工人的那份影响很沉，却从不想压人一头。他说，好活计自己会说话。"},"gross":{"tw":[["complete",0],["gate",3],["gain",2],["net",1],["increase",6],["perfect",0],["sum",2],["decrease",6],["rank",0]],"en":"The small company had to count its gross profit at the end of the year. The total sum was higher than last year, a real gain. After the costs, the net figure was much smaller. There was a slight increase in sales, but also a decrease in the price of goods. The manager said the market was not perfect. Two workers would check every number at the gate before sending the report. This small step could complete the whole account. In the end the firm moved up in rank. It was not a great year, but a fair one.","zh":"这家小公司得在年底算一算它的总利润。总数比去年高，是实实在在的增长。扣掉成本以后，净额就小多了。销量略有增加，货价却在下降。经理说，市场从来算不上完美。两名工人会在门口把每个数字核一遍，再送报告。这一小步能把整本账做完整。到头来，公司往上升了一个名次。这不是大年，却是个公道的年。"},"halt":{"tw":[["check",2],["settle",3],["pause",2],["suspend",6],["freeze",0],["stand",3],["prevent",2],["resume",6],["game",0]],"en":"Heavy snow brought the mountain road to a halt before noon. Drivers had to pause and check their tyres in the cold. The police would suspend all traffic until the wind settled. Ice could freeze on the bridge and prevent any safe pass. We had to stand by the fire and wait. Nobody spoke for a while, and the cold made the wait feel long. A small sign listed the game that was cancelled that night. By evening the trucks began to move again. The next bus would resume its route at dawn.","zh":"正午前，大雪把盘山公路逼停。司机们只好停下来，在冷风里检查轮胎。警察会先把所有车辆拦下，等风歇了再说。桥面上会结冰，让任何安全的通行都做不成。我们只好站在火堆边等。一块小牌子上写着当晚取消的那场比赛。到傍晚，卡车又开始动了。下一班车天亮时就恢复路线。"},"hazard":{"tw":[["chance",0],["suspect",3],["danger",2],["impact",6],["guess",0],["bunker",3],["try",2],["damage",6],["luck",0]],"en":"Loose rocks on the old path are a real hazard for any walker. We had to try the safe way around, though it was longer. There was little chance of a quick repair. My guide would suspect that a storm had moved the stones down, and he saw a clear danger in the wet ground. The impact of one falling rock could break a leg. A single guess about the weather could put us in trouble. We took shelter in a small bunker by the mine. In the end the damage to the path was small, and we counted our luck.","zh":"老路上松动的石头对任何行路人都是真正的危险。我们只好试着绕安全的那条，虽然远些。短时间内修好的可能不大。向导怀疑是一场风暴把石头冲了下来，他在湿地上看出明显的凶险。一块滚下来的石头砸中，就能打断一条腿。对天气的一次乱猜就可能让我们陷入麻烦。我们躲进矿边一座小掩体里。最后小路上的破坏不大，我们算自己运气好。"},"impact":{"tw":[["touch",0],["blow",3],["change",2],["result",6],["affect",0],["hit",3],["fight",2],["effect",6],["shock",0]],"en":"The heavy flood had a deep impact on the small village. Its effect could be seen in every broken road. The first blow came at night, when the water began to touch the lowest houses. That single night would change many lives and affect the whole year. The fight to save the bridge left two men hurt from a hard hit. The shock of the loss was slow to leave. In the end the result was better than we feared. Some families left the village for good. The rest rebuilt, and its people grew closer.","zh":"那场大水给这个小村子带来很深的冲击。它的影响在每条断掉的路上一眼就能看见。头一记重击是夜里来的，水开始碰到最矮的几户人家。那一夜会改变许多人的生活，也影响这一年。为保住桥的那场拼斗，让两个男人挨了重重一下。这场失去带来的震动久久不散。到头来结果比我们担心的要好。村子重建了，人们的心也更近了。"},"impose":{"tw":[["visit",0],["lay",3],["charge",2],["sanction",6],["inflict",0],["order",3],["communicate",2],["limit",6],["levy",0]],"en":"The town decided to impose a small tax on every new building. They would levy a fair charge on the big shops and lay the money aside for the school. The council had to communicate the plan before the vote. Some owners would order a delay, but the law was clear. The council could sanction the tax only after a second vote. A strict limit was set on the tallest walls. No one wanted to inflict harm on small families, so the rule spared them. The mayor would visit each street to explain.","zh":"镇里决定对每一栋新房子加征一小笔税。他们会对大商铺收一笔公道的费用，把钱留出来给学校。议会得在投票前把这套方案跟大家说清楚。有些业主会想来拖一拖，可规定很清楚。要经过第二次表决，议会才能批准这项税。最高的墙被定了一个严格的限度。没人愿意伤害小家庭，所以这条规矩放过了他们。镇长会挨条街去解释。"},"destruction":{"tw":[["destroy",4],["death",0],["kill",3],["terror",6],["demolition",3],["ruin",3],["invasion",6]],"en":"The great storm of that autumn brought destruction to the whole valley. It seemed ready to destroy every field and to kill the young trees. People watched from the hill in silence and in terror, afraid of the death of their small farms. After the water went down, a team began the demolition of two unsafe houses. The ruin of the old mill stood alone by the river. Some families spoke of it as an invasion of water, not of men. In spring, new grass covered the ground. Nobody in the village forgot that night.","zh":"那年秋天的大风暴给整个山谷带来了破坏。它像是要把每一片田都毁掉，把那些小树都杀死。人们站在山上，又沉默又恐惧，害怕自家的小农场就这样没了。水退之后，一队人开始拆掉两栋不安全的房子。老磨坊的废墟孤零零地立在河边。有些人家说，这是水的侵袭，不是人的。到了春天，新草盖住了地面。那一夜，村里没人会忘。"},"essential":{"tw":[["essence",4],["necessary",5],["need",3],["vital",6],["crucial",0],["basic",6],["necessity",0]],"en":"Clean water is essential for any village, and in the dry south it is truly vital. The doctor said that for a sick child, water is more crucial than any medicine. At its essence, health is simple: food, rest, and clean air. People often forget the basic things and chase what is not necessary at all. In that small clinic the greatest need was a pump, not a machine. Even a plain bar of soap became a daily necessity. Once the well was fixed, fewer children fell ill. That winter the whole town understood the lesson.","zh":"干净的水对任何村子都必不可少，在干旱的南方更是性命攸关。医生说，对一个生病的孩子，水比任何药都要紧。说到底，健康很简单：食物、休息和干净的空气。人们常常忘了最基本的几样，反倒去追那些根本不必要的东西。在那间小诊所里，最需要的是一台水泵，而不是什么机器。连一块普通肥皂都成了每天的必需品。水井修好之后，生病的孩子就少了。那个冬天，全镇的人都懂了这个道理。"},"evolve":{"tw":[["evolution",4],["develop",2],["derive",3],["change",2],["adapt",6],["germinate",0],["flourish",6]],"en":"A single seed can evolve into a tall tree, though the change is far too slow to see. In the long story of evolution, a plant will develop new ways to find light. Some will derive their food from the air and adapt to a dry land. In spring the first leaves germinate under the wet soil, and by summer the whole wood begins to flourish. My teacher said that a garden is a small picture of a forest. She let us watch one seed for a month. Nothing happened for two weeks, then a green line appeared.","zh":"一粒种子能长成一棵大树，只是这变化慢得看不出来。在漫长的演化过程里，植物会慢慢长出寻找阳光的新办法。有的会从空气里获取养分，并适应干旱的土地。春天，最先的叶子在湿润的土里发芽，到夏天整片林子都开始茂盛起来。老师说，一座花园就是一片森林的缩影。她让我们盯着一粒种子看了一个月。头两个星期什么都没发生，后来冒出了一道绿线。"},"expenditure":{"tw":[["expend",4],["consumption",0],["cost",3],["fiscal",6],["outlay",0],["expense",3],["revenue",6]],"en":"At the end of the year the small firm had to look hard at its expenditure. The cost of power had risen, and the total outlay for new machines was far too high. My father, who keeps the books, said they must expend less on travel and watch the daily consumption of paper. The fiscal report showed a small rise in revenue, but not enough. He cut every needless expense and wrote a new budget on one page. By the next spring the numbers were green again. The owner thanked him with a quiet nod.","zh":"到了年底，这家小公司不得不认真看看自己的开支。电费涨了，买新机器的总支出又高得离谱。管账的爸爸说，出差要少花钱，纸张每天的消耗也得盯着。财务报告显示收入略有增加，可还是不够。他把每一笔不必要的费用都砍掉，用一页纸重新做了预算。到第二年春天，账上的数字又好看了。老板朝他默默地点了点头。"},"frequent":{"tw":[["frequency",4],["shop",0],["support",2],["sporadic",6],["sponsor",0],["brief",6],["haunt",0]],"en":"The little music shop on our street held a concert every month, and the crowd was frequent and warm. Because the visits were so frequent, the owner could plan the whole year. He would sponsor a young player now and then, and his support meant a lot to them. The shows were not sporadic; they came like clockwork. Once an old singer came back to haunt the small room for one brief night, and the place was full. He kept a note of the frequency of every song the people asked for. That small shop, he said, was his whole life.","zh":"我们街上那家小乐器店每月都办一场演出，来的人多而热络。因为来客这么经常，老板能把一整年都排好。他时不时会资助一个年轻乐手，这份支持对他们很重要。演出并不零散，来得像钟表一样准。有一回一位老歌手回来，在这间小屋里演了短短一个晚上，店里坐得满满的。他记下人们点唱的每首歌出现的次数。他说，这家小店就是他的一辈子。"},"define":{"tw":[["fix",0],["quantify",3],["choose",2],["context",6],["determine",3],["reset",3],["dictate",6],["specify",2]],"en":"Before we began the project, the leader asked us to define every goal in plain words. We had to fix the limits first and then quantify each one with a number. She said we should choose a small aim, not a wide one, and write it down. The context of the whole market would determine how far we could go. If the plan went wrong, we could reset it and start again. No one could dictate the result to us. She told us to specify the day we would finish. We worked late, but the plan was clear.","zh":"项目开始之前，负责人让我们用大白话把每个目标都定清楚。我们得先划定界限，再用一个数字把每一项量化。她说目标要选小的，别选得太宽，还要写下来。整个市场的大环境会决定我们能走多远。要是计划走偏了，我们可以重新设定，再从头来。结果不是谁能命令出来的。她让我们把完工的日子明确写出来。我们干到很晚，但方案很清楚。"},"dimension":{"tw":[["attribute",0],["feature",3],["mark",2],["element",6],["proportion",0],["quality",3],["shape",2],["infinite",6]],"en":"When we design a room, the most important dimension is not its length but its light. Every element of the space must be in the right proportion to the others. A good feature of the old house was the tall window, and its shape had a quiet quality. My teacher would mark each drawing with a small number for scale. He said a house has another attribute that no ruler can measure: the way it feels. Space can seem almost infinite in a room with no walls. We worked on the plan all morning.","zh":"设计一间屋子的时候，最重要的尺寸不是长度，而是光。空间里的每个元素都该和别的元素成合适的比例。那栋老房子一个很好的特征就是那扇高窗，它的形状透着一种安静的气质。老师会在每张图上标一个小数字表示比例。他说房子还有一种量尺量不出的属性：它给人的感觉。没有墙的屋子里，空间几乎显得无边无际。这个方案我们做了一上午。"},"disagree":{"tw":[["differ",0],["contradict",3],["agree",1],["argue",6],["dissent",3],["clash",3],["concur",6],["discord",0]],"en":"My father and my uncle disagree about almost everything, and their talks often end in discord. They differ on money, on work, and even on the colour of a door. One will argue for an hour, and the other will contradict every word. Yet when it comes to family, they agree on the important things. A neighbour said it was a clash of two strong men, and he did not concur with either. My uncle would dissent only to make a point. Still, at dinner they passed the bread and laughed.","zh":"我爸和我叔叔几乎什么都谈不拢，聊着聊着就闹得不欢而散。钱上、工作上，连门漆什么颜色都能各执一词。一个能争上一个钟头，另一个就逐句反驳。可一说到家里的事，重要的地方两人又是一致的。邻居说这是两个硬脾气撞在一起，而他对谁都不赞成。我叔叔有时只是为了表明立场才唱反调。可到了饭桌上，他们还是把面包递给对方，笑了。"},"display":{"tw":[["expose",0],["open",3],["disclosure",2],["image",6],["exhibit",0],["sight",3],["woo",2],["screen",6]],"en":"At the small museum the display of old clocks filled a whole room. Each exhibit stood behind glass, and every image was lit from above. The door was left open so that people could come and go. The curator said the aim was to expose the young to old work, not to woo rich buyers. A sudden disclosure in the paper brought more visitors than before. Through the screen by the door, one could see the whole hall, a fine sight at night. We stayed until closing. I bought a small card and sent it to my sister.","zh":"在小小的博物馆里，老钟表的陈列摆满了整整一间屋。每件展品都立在玻璃后面，每张图像都从上方打着光。大门敞开着，让人随便进出。馆长说，他们是想让年轻人接触老手艺，不是为了招揽有钱的买家。报上一则突然的披露，让来的人比平时多了不少。从门口那块屏幕看进去，整个大厅尽收眼底，夜里看格外好。我们一直待到闭馆。我买了一张小卡片，寄给了我妹妹。"},"echo":{"tw":[["ring",0],["parrot",3],["reply",2],["faint",6],["recall",0],["sound",2],["loud",6],["repeat",0]],"en":"In the empty hall my shout came back as a long echo. The sound would ring from wall to wall and repeat twice before it died. A boy near the door would reply with a louder call, and the whole room seemed to shake. A grey parrot in the corner tried to recall the noise and copy it. Even a faint whisper could travel far in that air. 'It is like a talking house,' my cousin said. We had to whisper on the way out. Later I told the story to my class at school.","zh":"在空荡荡的大厅里，我一喊，回音长长地弹回来。那声音在四壁之间回荡，还要重上一遍才消失。门边一个男孩用更响的一声回应，整间屋子好像都在抖。角落里一只灰鹦鹉想学那声音，跟着叫。在那样的空气里，连极轻的一句话也能传得很远。'这简直像一栋会说话的房子，'我表妹说。出来的时候，我们只好小声说话。后来我把这件事讲给了班上的同学听。"},"eliminate":{"tw":[["pass",0],["cut",3],["kill",2],["rid",6],["eradicate",0],["exclude",3],["destroy",2],["extinguish",0]],"en":"The village hoped to eliminate a fever that came every summer with the rain. To rid the houses of the insects, workers had to cut the tall grass by the water. They would exclude no family and check every yard. A hard plan could destroy the breeding ground and kill the young flies. Some farmers feared the spray would extinguish the bees as well. Pass the word, the doctor said, and let the whole town take part. It took three years, but they did eradicate the disease at last. The next summer was quiet and cool.","zh":"村里想彻底除掉一种每到雨季就来的热病。为了把虫子从屋里赶走，工人们得把水边的长草割掉。他们一户不落，逐个检查院子。一个够狠的办法能把蚊虫的孳生地毁掉，也能杀死那些幼虫。有些农民担心，药水会把蜜蜂也一起灭了。医生说，把话传出去，让全镇的人都参与。整整三年，他们终于把这种病根除了。接下来的那个夏天，安静又凉爽。"},"encounter":{"tw":[["chance",0],["confront",3],["fight",2],["clash",6],["find",0],["intersect",3],["tense",6],["meet",0]],"en":"On a mountain trail I had a strange encounter with an old man at noon. There was little chance we would meet in such a wild place, yet our paths had to intersect at that rock. He seemed to want to confront me at first, and for a moment the air was tense. We did not fight, and there was no clash of words. I offered him water and bread, and we sat down on the warm stone. Later I could not find the same path again. It was a meeting I never forgot.","zh":"在山间小路上，中午我和一位老人有了一次奇怪的相遇。在这样荒僻的地方，我们碰上的机会微乎其微，可两条路偏偏就在那块石头处交汇了。起初他像是想跟我对上，那一瞬间空气都紧绷起来。我们没动手，也没有言语上的冲突。我分给他水和面包，两人坐在温热的石头上。后来我再也没找到那条路。这次相遇我一直记着。"},"endorse":{"tw":[["back",0],["visa",3],["sign",2],["agree",6],["second",0],["approve",2],["accept",6],["support",2]],"en":"The club asked a well-known coach to endorse their summer camp. He had to sign a short letter and agree to lend his name. The committee would second the idea and approve the whole plan at once. His support meant that many parents would accept the offer. A man from the office had to check the visa of one worker, then back the group's choice. In the end the coach came for one day and played with the children. That single visit helped the camp more than any poster. He said he would come again next summer.","zh":"俱乐部请一位有名的教练为他们的夏令营背书。他得签一封短信，同意借用自己的名字。委员会附议这个想法，立刻通过了整个方案。有了他的支持，许多家长都愿意接受这个安排。办公室里有个人要核对一名工人的签证，然后再为小组的选择撑腰。最后教练来了一天，陪孩子们玩。就这一趟，比任何海报都管用。他说，明年夏天他还会再来。"},"ensure":{"tw":[["insure",0],["cover",3],["verify",2],["maintain",6],["secure",0],["doom",3],["establish",6],["assure",0]],"en":"Before the rainy season, we had to ensure that the old roof would hold. My father wanted to insure the house and to cover the cost of any damage. He asked a worker to verify every tile and to secure the loose ones at once. It was hard to maintain the whole roof alone, so he called two friends. 'If we do nothing, we doom the whole room to water,' he said. He could not assure us that it would be easy. But that afternoon they did establish a dry, safe house for the winter.","zh":"雨季之前，我们得保证那面旧屋顶撑得住。我爸想给房子投保，把万一的损失也覆盖上。他让一个工人把每片瓦都查一遍，松动的地方立刻固定好。整个屋顶一个人很难维护，于是他又叫来两个朋友。他说：'要是我们什么也不做，就等于把整间屋子交给雨水。'他不敢向我们保证这事轻松。可那天下午，他们真的为过冬弄出了一间干燥、安全的屋子。"},"estimate":{"tw":[["figure",0],["allow",3],["respect",2],["survey",6],["guess",3],["evaluate",2],["forecast",6],["judge",0]],"en":"Before the bridge work began, the engineer gave a careful estimate of the cost. The figure was much higher than the first guess, and no one was happy. He asked us to allow for bad weather and to respect the old stone. A short survey of the river would help us evaluate the risk. The forecast said the water would rise in March. A good judge of such things, he said, never trusts one number alone. In the end we cut the plan in half. The new price was still high, but we could live with it.","zh":"动工修桥之前，工程师给了一份仔细的费用估算。这个数目比最初的猜测高出不少，谁都不太高兴。他让我们把坏天气也算进去，还要顾惜那些老石头。对河做一次简短的勘测，有助于我们评估风险。预报说三月河水会上涨。他说，真正懂行的人从不只信一个数字。最后我们把方案砍掉了一半。新价钱还是偏高，但我们能接受。"},"exhibit":{"tw":[["present",0],["open",3],["walk",2],["garden",6],["expose",0],["model",3],["mural",6],["march",0]],"en":"For the spring exhibit the school opened its garden to the whole town. Each class had to present one piece of work and to explain it to the visitors. We would walk along the wall where a long mural had been painted by hand. A small model of the old market stood in the middle of the grass. The aim was to expose young artists to a real audience, not to sell anything. In the afternoon a band led a short march around the field. My sister's picture was the first one people saw.","zh":"春季展览那几天，学校把花园向全镇开放。每个班都要拿出一件作品，还要向来客讲一讲。我们沿着那面墙走，墙上一幅长长的壁画是手工画的。草地中央立着一个老集市的小模型。这样做是想让年轻的艺术作者面对真正的观众，而不是为了卖东西。下午一支乐队带着大家绕着场地走了一小圈。我妹妹的画，是人们最先看到的那幅。"},"extract":{"tw":[["express",0],["cut",3],["choose",2],["juice",6],["pull",0],["thread",3],["paste",6],["evoke",0]],"en":"To make the drink, my aunt would extract the juice from a pile of fresh fruit. She had to cut each one open and choose the ripe ones first. Then she would pull the soft flesh apart with her hands and press it through cloth. A long thread of syrup ran into the jug. She liked to paste a small note on the bottle to express the day it was made. The smell would evoke the whole summer garden. We drank it slowly on the step. That bottle did not last a single day.","zh":"为了做那瓶饮料，姑妈会从一堆新鲜水果里榨出汁来。她得把每个都切开，先挑熟透的。然后用双手把软软的果肉撕开，隔着布挤压。一缕浓稠的糖浆流进罐子里。她喜欢在瓶子上贴一张小纸条，写明是哪天做的。那股香味会唤起整个夏天的花园。我们坐在台阶上，慢慢把它喝完。那瓶东西连一天都没撑住。"},"factor":{"tw":[["agent",0],["fundamental",3],["cause",2],["negative",6],["component",0],["parameter",3],["difference",6],["element",0]],"en":"The doctor said sleep is the main factor in a child's growth. A lack of it is a negative element that can cause real trouble at school. Even one small parameter, like the hour of bedtime, can make a difference. The fundamental cause, she said, is often a screen in the bedroom. A healthy diet is another component of the same picture. A good agent of change is the parent who turns the light off early. She told us to watch these things for a month. It worked better than we expected.","zh":"医生说，睡眠是孩子长身体最主要的因素。睡不够是一个负面的因素，会在学校惹出真正的麻烦。哪怕只是一个小参数，比如几点上床，也能带来差别。她说，根本的原因往往是卧室里那块屏幕。健康的饮食是同一幅画里的另一个组成部分。推动改变的一个好角色，是那个早早关灯的家长。她让我们观察这些一个月。效果比我们预想的还好。"},"foster":{"tw":[["further",0],["serve",3],["encourage",2],["partner",6],["nurture",0],["rear",2],["care",6],["surrogate",0]],"en":"My aunt chose to foster two children after her own had grown up. She wanted to nurture them as a partner with the local office, not as a surrogate mother alone. It took patience to rear a child who had known little care. She would encourage every small step and serve them a warm meal each night. To further their studies, she kept a small box of books by the door. People said she was brave; she said she was only kind. Both children stayed until they found work. The house was never quiet again.","zh":"姑妈在自家孩子长大以后，选择收养了两个孩子。她想和当地的机构一起把他们带大，而不是只做一个替代的母亲。把一个没怎么被疼过的孩子抚养成人，需要极大的耐心。她鼓励他们每一点进步，每晚给他们端上一顿热饭。为了让他们的学业更进一步，她在门边放了一个装书的小箱子。人们说她勇敢；她说她只是心软。两个孩子一直住到找着了工作。这屋子从此再没安静过。"},"fulfil":{"tw":[["fill",0],["run",3],["complete",2],["realise",6],["meet",2],["suffice",3],["effect",2],["satisfy",0]],"en":"My father promised to fulfil one last wish for his old teacher. He had to fill a small room with books and to run the little library alone. It took two years to complete the work, and many evenings were long. He did realise at last how much it had cost him. To meet the cost, he sold a watch that he loved. A small grant had to suffice for the rest. The effect on the village was greater than anyone guessed. In the end he did satisfy the promise he had made.","zh":"我爸答应为他年迈的老师完成最后一个心愿。他得把一间小屋装满书，还要一个人照看这个小图书馆。这项工作花了两年才做完，很多个晚上都很漫长。到最后他才真正明白，这让他付出了多大的代价。为了凑钱，他把一块心爱的手表卖了。剩下的一点，只够靠一小笔资助撑着。这件事对村子的影响，比谁猜的都要大。最后他到底还是兑现了当初许下的诺言。"},"heal":{"tw":[["cure",0],["granulate",3],["better",2],["overcome",6],["mend",0],["recuperate",3],["help",2],["regenerate",6]],"en":"After the long illness, it took my grandfather a whole winter to heal. The doctor said no quick cure could help a body so tired. A slow rest was the only way to overcome it, and to mend what the fever had broken. Each day the wound would granulate a little and the skin grow new. He had to sit in the sun to recuperate and let time do its work. By March he felt better than he had in years. He said the body can regenerate if you give it a chance.","zh":"那场大病之后，我爷爷用了整整一个冬天才养好。医生说，这么虚的身体，什么灵药也帮不上忙。唯一的办法是慢慢休息，把高烧弄坏的地方一点点修补回来。伤口每天长出一点新肉，皮肤也慢慢更新。他只能坐在太阳底下静养，让时间去起作用。到三月，他感觉比这些年里任何时候都好。他说，只要你给它机会，身体是能自我修复的。"},"ideal":{"tw":[["saint",0],["value",3],["idea",4],["simple",6],["idealistic",0],["exemplar",3],["model",2],["concept",6]],"en":"In class we talked about the ideal of a good life. Our teacher said that a saint is not the only exemplar we can follow. Her own idealistic view was simple: help those near you before you dream of far places. The old nurse in our town became a model for many students. She held the value of patience above praise, and she never chased a prize. The concept of service, she said, was her whole idea of work. We wrote her a letter that spring. She kept it in her pocket for years.","zh":"课上我们谈到什么是理想的人生。老师说，圣人并不是我们唯一可以效法的榜样。她自己那种带点理想色彩的想法很简单：先帮好身边的人，再去想远方的事。镇上那位老护士成了许多学生的榜样。她把耐心看得比赞美更重，从不追逐什么奖项。她说，服务的理念就是她对工作的全部想法。那年春天我们给她写了一封信。她把信揣在口袋里放了好多年。"},"implement":{"tw":[["apply",0],["bar",3],["complete",2],["propose",6],["enforce",0],["run",3],["use",2],["plan",6]],"en":"The council wanted to implement a new rule about waste in the market. They had to propose the plan in public first, then enforce it from June. A metal bar would be fixed at the gate to keep the carts out. Every seller had to apply for a small card and to use the new bins daily. It took a month to complete the change, and some people were slow to follow. My aunt, who runs a fruit stall, said the rule was fair. In the end the street was much cleaner.","zh":"议会想在集市上实施一条关于垃圾的新规定。他们得先公开提出方案，再从六月起执行。门口会装一根铁栏杆，把板车挡在外面。每个摊贩都得申请一张小卡片，每天用新的垃圾桶。这项改动花了一个月才完成，有些人跟得比较慢。卖水果的姑妈说，这条规矩是公道的。最后，那条街干净多了。"},"deliberate":{"tw":[["consider",0],["see",3],["justify",6],["debate",3],["wrestle",3],["tactic",6],["moot",0]],"en":"The committee had to make a deliberate choice about the new road. They would consider every letter from the villagers and debate each point for a full evening. One member tried to justify the plan with old maps, but the numbers did not hold. Another would wrestle with the cost for hours, unable to decide. The tactic of waiting for more facts was fair, yet the town was growing impatient. Some said the whole question was moot, since the money had already been spent. 'You can see the gap,' said the chair, 'between what we want and what we can pay for.' In the end they chose to wait one more month.","zh":"委员会得就那条新路做一个深思熟虑的决定。他们要把村民来的每一封信都考虑进去，还要花上整整一个晚上逐条辩论。有位委员想用旧地图为方案辩护，可数字站不住脚。另一位则对着花销纠结了好几个小时，拿不定主意。等更多事实再说的办法是稳妥的，可镇上已经越来越不耐烦了。有人说，钱既然已经花出去了，这个问题根本没有讨论的意义。主席说：'你们看得见那条缝——我们想要的和我们付得起的之间。'最后他们决定再等一个月。"},"despite":{"tw":[["contempt",0],["dislike",2],["over",6],["disdain",0],["disregard",2],["result",6],["scorn",0]],"en":"The old gardener worked for years under the despite of everyone at the big house. The young owner would show him open contempt and speak to him as if he were a tool. In return the gardener felt a quiet dislike for the man, though he never said a word. Over the table one evening the owner showed pure disdain for the small garden and ordered it pulled up. The gardener chose to disregard the order and kept the roses alive. The result was that the flowers won a prize that autumn. The owner could only watch with scorn as the neighbours praised the old man.","zh":"那位老园丁在大宅里干了多年，一直被人轻贱。年轻的东家对他露出毫不掩饰的轻蔑，跟他说话像对一件工具。园丁心里则对这人存着一份淡淡的厌恶，却一个字也没说过。一天傍晚在饭桌上，东家对那座小花园满是不屑，下令把它铲掉。园丁选择不理这个命令，把那些玫瑰留了下来。结果那年秋天，这些花得了个奖。邻居们夸起这位老人时，东家只能在旁边带着讥讽看着。"},"devastate":{"tw":[["waste",0],["ruin",3],["destroy",2],["cripple",6],["ravage",0],["overwhelm",2],["engulf",6]],"en":"A great flood came down the valley and seemed to devastate everything in its path. It would destroy the small bridge first and then swallow the fields whole. In an hour the water could engulf the lower street and turn the harvest into waste. The storm did not just ruin the crops; it would cripple the mill that gave the village its work. Old families watched the flood ravage the shops they had built over a lifetime. The scale of the loss was enough to overwhelm even the calmest neighbour. By morning the river was quiet again, and people began to count what was left.","zh":"一场大水顺着山谷冲下来，仿佛要把它经过的一切都毁掉。它先冲垮那座小桥，接着把田地整个吞下去。一个小时之内，水就能淹掉下面那条街，把收成变成一堆废弃之物。这场风暴不只是毁了庄稼，它还打断了给村里提供活计的那家磨坊。几户老住户眼看着洪水糟蹋掉他们一辈子盖起来的店铺。损失之大，连最沉得住气的邻居都招架不住。到早晨，河又安静下来，人们开始清点剩下些什么。"},"dictate":{"tw":[["order",0],["mandate",3],["read",2],["define",6],["prescribe",0],["rule",2],["interpret",6]],"en":"The old manager liked to dictate his letters instead of writing them. Each morning he would order his assistant to sit down, and then he would read the words aloud, slowly and clearly. She had to define each term exactly as he wished and never to interpret his meaning on her own. His rule was simple: nothing left the office without his name. A new mandate from the head office, however, said that all letters must be signed by two people. The manager did not like it, but he had to follow what the rule prescribed for every branch. After a week he grew used to it.","zh":"那位老经理喜欢口述信件，而不是自己写。每天早上他都会叫助理坐下，然后慢慢地把字句念出来，清清楚楚。她必须按他的意思把每个词都定得准确，绝不能自作主张去解释。他的规矩很简单：没有他名字的东西一律不许出办公室。可总部来的一道新指令说，所有信件都必须有两个人签字。经理不喜欢，但他只好照着这条规矩对每个部门执行。过了一个星期，他也习惯了。"},"disc":{"tw":[["record",0],["token",3],["circle",2],["stereo",6],["platter",0],["plate",2],["feature",6]],"en":"My uncle kept an old disc in a paper sleeve beside his stereo. It was a record of songs from a small band that no one remembered now. The disc was a perfect circle, and its silver platter caught the light when he turned it. Each track had one special feature: a short whistle that ran under the tune. He would clean it with a soft cloth and lay it on the plate of the player as if it were a token of luck. When the music began, the whole room grew quiet. That single disc held a whole summer of his youth.","zh":"我叔叔把一张旧唱片收在纸套里，就放在他的音响旁边。那是一个没人记得的小乐队录的歌。唱片是个完美的圆，他转动它的时候，银色的唱盘会反光。每一首曲子都有一个特别之处：旋律底下藏着一声短短的口哨。他会用软布把它擦干净，再像放一枚幸运符一样把它搁在唱机上。音乐一响，整个房间都静了下来。就这一张唱片，装着他年少时的一整个夏天。"},"dose":{"tw":[["drug",0],["hit",3],["medicine",2],["acid",0],["poison",3],["process",2],["dot",0]],"en":"The nurse measured a small dose of the medicine into a glass cup. Too much of the same drug could act like a poison, so the process had to be exact. She placed a tiny dot of the liquid on a test strip first. The doctor had warned that a strong acid in the mixture could burn the throat, and one heavy hit of the wrong amount would do real harm. He watched her hands, then nodded. The boy drank it and made a face. Within an hour his fever had gone, and he asked for food.","zh":"护士把一小剂药量进一只玻璃杯里。同一种药用多了就成了毒，所以整个流程必须分毫不差。她先在试纸上滴了一小点药水。医生提醒过，混合物里有一种强酸会烧喉咙，量拿错一次重手就会造成真正的伤害。他盯着她的手，随后点了点头。男孩喝下去，做了个鬼脸。不到一个小时，他的烧就退了，还嚷着要吃东西。"},"emit":{"tw":[["breathe",0],["shoot",3],["absorb",1],["ultraviolet",6],["utter",0],["steam",3],["helium",6]],"en":"In the greenhouse the young scientist watched the plants emit a faint light. When the leaves absorb too much ultraviolet, they begin to breathe faster and give off a thin steam. A small camera on the roof would shoot a picture every minute and record the colour. The machine itself could utter a soft click each time the light changed. The team filled a clear tube with helium to keep the air dry. 'If a plant can signal trouble,' she said, 'a farmer can act sooner.' The experiment ran for a month, and the data looked clean.","zh":"在温室里，那位年轻科学家看着植物发出微弱的光。叶子吸收过多紫外线时，会开始加快呼吸，并冒出一股薄薄的蒸汽。屋顶上的一台小相机每分钟拍一张照片，把颜色记下来。机器的本身在光每次变化时会发出轻轻的一声咔哒。团队往一根透明管里充了氦气，好让空气保持干燥。'要是植物能报出毛病，'她说，'农民就能更早动手。'实验做了一个月，数据看起来很干净。"},"enforce":{"tw":[["implement",0],["run",3],["compel",2],["exempt",1],["violate",6],["execute",3],["circumvent",6]],"en":"When the new recycling rule came, the town had to enforce it in every street. The office would run a short campaign first and then implement the system block by block. Inspectors could compel a shop to sort its waste, but small kitchens were exempt for the first year. Anyone who chose to violate the rule twice would receive a fine. A few owners tried to circumvent the checks by hiding their bins at the back. The council said it would execute the plan slowly and fairly. After three months the amount of waste had fallen by a fifth.","zh":"新的回收规定出来以后，镇上得在每条街都把它落实下去。办公室先办一场小小的宣传，然后一个街区一个街区地把这套办法推起来。检查员可以强制商店把垃圾分类，但小餐馆头一年可以免除。谁要是两次违反这条规定，就得吃一张罚单。有几个店主想把垃圾桶藏到后面，以此绕开检查。镇议会说，这个计划会慢慢来，而且公平地执行。三个月后，垃圾的量少了五分之一。"},"exploit":{"tw":[["work",2],["hit",3],["manipulate",6],["tap",0],["milk",3],["potential",6],["feat",0]],"en":"The old sailor liked to tell one story about his greatest exploit. Years ago he had to tap a small hole in the ice and pull his boat through it, a feat no one else would try. The next morning he would milk the last goat on board to feed the crew. It was not luck but careful work that saved them. A single wrong move could hit the hull and let the sea in. He learned to manipulate the sails with one hand while the other held the rope. 'The sea tests your potential,' he said, 'and then it takes most of it back.'","zh":"那位老水手爱讲一个关于他最了不起的壮举的故事。多年前，他得在冰上凿开一个小洞，把船从里面拖过去，这事别人谁也不敢试。第二天早上，他把船上最后一只羊挤了奶，喂给船员吃。救他们的不是运气，而是细心的苦干。一步走错，就可能撞到船身，让海水灌进来。他学会了一只手摆弄船帆，另一只手攥着绳子。他说：'大海会试探你的潜力，然后又把大半都收回去。'"},"fade":{"tw":[["pass",0],["disappear",2],["vanish",6],["melt",0],["devolve",2],["stumble",6],["slice",0]],"en":"An old photograph on the shelf had begun to fade at the edges. As the years pass, the faces in it slowly disappear, until one winter the smallest figure seemed to vanish altogether. My mother would melt a little wax on the frame to keep the damp out, but it did not help much. She told me how one summer the family had seemed to devolve into small quarrels over nothing. On the day of the picture they were still happy, and no one would stumble or lose their smile. She would slice the photo from its paper backing and copy it at the shop. 'Now it will not go,' she said.","zh":"架子上那张旧照片的边缘开始褪色了。日子一年年过去，照片上的面孔慢慢消失，到有一个冬天，最小的那个人影好像完全不见了。我妈会在相框上化一点蜡，好挡住潮气，可也没多大用处。她跟我讲，有那么一个夏天，一家人好像渐渐退化成为了鸡毛蒜皮的小吵小闹。拍照那天他们还是快快乐乐的，没有人会绊倒，也没有人会丢掉笑容。她把照片从纸背上裁下来，拿到店里去翻印。'这下它就不会走了，'她说。"},"formal":{"tw":[["ball",0],["promenade",3],["dance",2],["informal",1],["presented",6],["gown",2],["request",6]],"en":"The town held a formal dance at the end of the school year. It was the one night when everyone wore a long gown and walked in a slow promenade through the hall. My sister said the whole event felt like a great ball from an old book. She had sent a written request to borrow a dress from a cousin. Two shy students made an informal deal to arrive together, then changed their minds twice. When the best dancer was presented with a small cup, she simply laughed. By midnight the band was tired and the music grew soft.","zh":"学年末，镇上办了一场正式的舞会。那是唯一一个晚上，人人都穿上长礼服，在大厅里慢慢地列队入场。我姐姐说，整场活动就像旧书里那种盛大的舞会。她早就写了一封请求信，想跟一位表姐借条裙子。两个腼腆的学生私下商量好一起来，后来又改了两回主意。当最会跳舞的那位被请上台领一只小杯子时，她只是笑。到了午夜，乐队累了，音乐也慢了下来。"},"former":{"tw":[["early",0],["first",2],["latter",1],["senior",6],["late",0],["veteran",6],["old",0]],"en":"Our former teacher came back to the school one last time before she moved away. In her early years she had taught in a room with a broken roof. She was the first woman in the village to finish a full course at the college. Now, older and slower, she met two of her old pupils at the gate. The late afternoon light fell on the senior class she had once led. A veteran of the war years, she never liked to talk about herself. Because of that, the latter part of her life stayed a mystery. We gave her a small plant and she promised to write.","zh":"我们从前的那位老师搬走之前，最后一次回了一趟学校。她早年教书时，教室的屋顶还是破的。她是村里第一个在学院读完完整课程的女性。如今，她年纪大了，动作也慢了，在门口和两个老学生碰了面。午后的斜阳落在她当年带过的毕业班上。她是经历过战争年代的老兵，却从不愿谈自己。正因如此，她后来那段人生始终是个谜。我们送了她一盆小植物，她答应会写信来。"},"fuel":{"tw":[["fire",3],["coke",3],["supply",2],["oil",6],["bunker",3],["stimulate",2],["reduce",6]],"en":"The winter was so cold that the family had to buy extra fuel for the old stove. They used oil most nights, and on the worst days a little coke to keep the fire alive. The supply in the barn was low, and the price had risen twice since autumn. My father would fill a bunker of coal by the back door so the wind could not reach it. He said the cold would stimulate the body at first, but never for long. To reduce the cost, they closed two rooms and lived in one. By March the last bag was empty and the garden began to wake.","zh":"那年冬天冷得厉害，一家人只好给老炉子多买些燃料。多数晚上他们烧油，最冷的日子再添一点焦炭，好让火别灭。谷仓里的存货不多了，入秋以来价钱已经涨了两次。我父亲会在后门边堆满一小仓煤，好让风够不着它。他说寒冷一开始会刺激身体，可从来撑不了多久。为了省下花销，他们关掉两间屋，全家人挤在一间里。到了三月，最后一袋也用完了，园子开始苏醒。"},"fundamental":{"tw":[["key",0],["factor",2],["principle",6],["cardinal",0],["harmonic",2],["context",6],["primal",0]],"en":"The music teacher began with a fundamental that every student had to know. The key to a good sound is not speed but a steady breath, and this one factor matters more than any trick. The same principle runs through every instrument, from the smallest flute to the largest drum. In that context the word cardinal simply means the most basic note of all. When two notes sound together, their harmonic waves either match or fight. Our primal fear of a wrong note, she said, only makes the hands shake. So we practised one long tone for a whole hour.","zh":"音乐老师从一个每个学生都必须知道的基本讲起。发出好声音的关键不是快，而是气息平稳，而这一点比任何技巧都重要。同一条原理贯穿每一件乐器，从最小的笛子到最大的鼓。放在这个语境里，所谓首要，无非就是指最基础的那个音。两个音一起响时，它们的谐波要么相合，要么相抗。她说，我们对吹错音那种本能的害怕，只会让手发抖。于是我们整整练了一个小时的长音。"},"harbor":{"tw":[["hold",0],["feel",2],["shore",6],["nurse",0],["hide",2],["bay",6],["entertain",0]],"en":"The little harbor lay quiet between two hills, and only a few boats still used it. On the shore a woman would nurse her small grandson while the men mended their nets. She said the bay had once been full of sails, and she liked to entertain the old sailors with stories when they came back. When a storm rose, every ship would hide behind the long wall and hold fast to its rope. It was hard not to feel safe there. 'A harbor is not the sea,' she said, 'and that is the whole point of it.'","zh":"那座小小的港口安安静静地躺在两座山之间，如今只有几条船还在用它。岸边，一个女人一边照看小孙子，一边看男人们补网。她说，这片海湾从前满是帆影，老人们回来时她爱拿故事来款待他们。风暴起来时，每条船都会躲到那道长堤后面，把缆绳抓得紧紧的。在那儿，人很难不觉得安心。她说：'港口不是海，而这正是它的意义所在。'"},"heel":{"tw":[["dog",0],["bottom",2],["toe",6],["list",0],["dance",2],["shoulder",6],["hound",0]],"en":"My cousin hurt her heel during the last dance class of the term. The doctor told her to rest, but a small dog at home kept running at her feet. Every step made her list to one side, like a boat about to turn over. She could feel the pain climb from her toe to her shoulder before the music even started. The bottom of her old shoe had cracked right through, and she had to borrow another pair. At home her neighbour's hound would wait by the gate and follow her to the corner. She missed two weeks, then came back and danced the whole piece.","zh":"我表妹在学期最后一堂舞蹈课上把脚后跟弄伤了。医生让她休息，可家里那只小狗老是往她脚边冲。每走一步，她就往一边歪，像条快要翻掉的船。音乐还没响，她就能感到疼痛从脚趾一直爬到了肩膀。她那双旧鞋的鞋底裂了个透，只好另借一双。在家时，邻居家的猎狗总在大门口等着，跟她走到街角。她缺了两周课，后来又回来把整支舞跳完了。"},"hint":{"tw":[["lead",0],["intimate",3],["faint",6],["suggest",0],["spark",3],["whiff",6],["touch",0]],"en":"My sister gave me one small hint about the party she was planning. She did not want to suggest too much, so she only said that I should keep Saturday free. The faint smell of a cake in the kitchen was enough to spark my curiosity. Then she let slip one word that seemed to intimate there would be a guest from far away. I caught a whiff of her perfume as she left the room, and her hand touched mine for a moment. That single touch and that one lead were all I needed. 'Do not tell anyone,' she said, and I promised.","zh":"关于她要办的那场聚会，我姐姐只给了我一个小小的暗示。她不想透露太多，只说让我把周六空出来。厨房里蛋糕的一缕淡香，就足以勾起我的好奇。接着她漏出一个词，好像在暗示会有一位远道而来的客人。她离开房间时，我闻到一股她的香水味，她的手在我手上碰了一下。就那轻轻一碰，还有那一条线索，对我已经够了。'别告诉别人，'她说，我答应了。"},"host":{"tw":[["horde",0],["feast",3],["bread",2],["parasite",1],["event",6],["computer",2],["world",6]],"en":"My aunt was the host of the biggest feast in our street that autumn. A whole horde of cousins arrived at noon, and by two the table was covered with bread, soup and fruit. She had planned the event for weeks and would not sit down once. A quiet guest sat in the corner with a small computer, taking photos for the family. Later my uncle called him a parasite because he ate four plates and helped with nothing. Still, he sent the pictures to the whole world that same night. My aunt only laughed and said a good host feeds everyone.","zh":"那个秋天，我姑妈是我们这条街上最大一场宴席的主人。一大群表亲中午就到了，到两点，桌上摆满了面包、汤和水果。这场活动她张罗了好几个星期，自己却一次也没坐下。一位安静的客人抱着台小电脑坐在角落里，替全家人拍照。后来我叔叔说他是个白吃白喝的家伙，吃了四盘菜，什么忙都没帮。可当晚他还把照片发给了全世界的人看。我姑妈只是笑，说好主人得让每个人都吃饱。"},"humour":{"tw":[["temper",0],["blood",3],["message",2],["wry",6],["fun",3],["quality",2],["irreverent",6]],"en":"The old comic had a humour that no one could copy. His temper was calm even on a bad night, and his jokes had a wry turn that made people think twice. He would send the same short message to the club every week: 'Keep the lights low and the fun high.' The quality of his voice, dry and slow, mattered as much as the words. Some found him irreverent, yet he never hurt anyone. He liked to say that good blood and a warm room can fix more than medicine. When he left the stage, the whole hall was still laughing.","zh":"那位老笑匠的幽默谁也没法学。就算碰上不顺心的晚上，他的脾气也很平稳，他的笑料带着一股冷峭的转折，让人多想两遍。他每周都会给俱乐部发同样一条短信：'灯放暗些，乐子放大些。'他那副又干又慢的嗓子的质地，和词句本身一样重要。有人觉得他没规没矩，可他从不伤人。他爱说，好血性加一间暖屋子，比药还管用。他下台的时候，满大厅的人都还在笑。"},"index":{"tw":[["power",0],["degree",3],["finger",2],["benchmark",6],["exponent",0],["list",2],["composite",6]],"en":"The teacher asked us to build a simple index of the prices in our town. To do that we had to list twenty goods and give each one a power of ten as its weight. Then we made a composite figure that could show the change by degree, month after month. The result became a benchmark for the whole class and a small point of pride for our school. One student raised a finger and asked why milk counted so much. The teacher answered with a smile: the price of milk is its clearest exponent. The final index rose by only two points, but the work taught us more than a book.","zh":"老师让我们给小镇上的物价编一个简单的指数。要做到这一点，我们得列出二十样商品，再给每样一个十的幂当权重。然后我们做出一个综合的数字，用来显示逐月变化到什么程度。这个结果成了全班的基准，也成了我们学校一点小小的骄傲。有个学生举起一根手指，问为什么牛奶占的分量那么大。老师笑着回答：牛奶的价格就是家庭开销最典型的代表。最后的指数只涨了两个点，可这份作业教给我们的比一本书还多。"}}});
